======================================================================
crypt_sha256.c, crypt_sha512.c, crypt_blowfish.c
======================================================================

Public domain. crypt_sha256.c and crypt_sha512.c say so in their own headers,
and crypt_blowfish.c says "No copyright is claimed, and the software is
hereby placed in the public domain". None of the three requires a notice to
travel with a binary, which is why they are listed here rather than above.

crypt_blowfish.c adds that if that disclaimer is ever deemed void, the
software is Copyright (c) 1998-2014 Solar Designer and released under terms
permitting redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or
without modification. That fallback grants no less than the public domain
dedication does, so the notice above is the one a redistributor has to carry.
